    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Refuse `==` in the edit file\n\nLAWP’s `ast` check is a **substring** search, not a real parser pass. Treat it as a stand-in for a linter.\n\nWrite `same(a, b)` with `===`. Print `false` for `0` and `\"\"`."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "ast-honest",
      "promptMd": "This lesson’s `==` ban is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "eslint",
          "md": "A full ESLint run"
        },
        {
          "id": "substr",
          "md": "A stand-in: the file text must not use `==`"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "substr"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "no-double",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.js",
      "promptMd": "> `same(0, \"\")` is false via `===`. Print `false`.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/main.js",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.js",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "stdout",
          "equals": "false"
        },
        {
          "type": "ast",
          "query": "==="
        },
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
